# Kan tickets

Board: [vtt](https://kan.bn/boards/y0t45eyjddnf). Ticket ids are `VTT-<cardNumber>`. CLI: `npm run kan` (see `docs/kan-integration.md`). Requires `KAN_API_KEY` in root `.env`.

## Agent workflow

When asked to do / work / finish a ticket:

1. Read the card (`npm run kan -- card VTT-n`); update the description if scope, clarifications, or testing notes change.
2. Move **backlog → in-progress** when starting implementation.
3. Implement and run verification (`build`, `test`, `lint`, `test:e2e`).
4. Add a **Resolution** section to the card description (what the issue was; what you fixed). Use `npm run kan -- set-description VTT-n --file …` if easier than inline edits.
5. Move **in-progress → done** after verification passes and the Resolution section is written.
6. Commit / push / open a PR only when the user asks (existing rule). Commit messages must start with `VTT-<n>:` (e.g. `VTT-42: Fix token animation snap`).

## Multi-ticket work items (MTWI)

- Titles: `[Slug] Specific subtask` (e.g. `[Engine Peel] Data panel config`).
- Every related ticket description includes the same `Branch: <branch-name>`.
- One shared branch and one PR to `main` for the whole MTWI; per-ticket commits still use each ticket’s `VTT-n`.

## Ticket content

- Concise title and description of the work.
- Keep the description current when work changes.
- Description must include a **Testing** section listing new/updated tests that guard the fix or support the feature.
- On completion, description must include a **Resolution** section: what the issue was (symptom / root cause) and what was fixed (concrete changes). Add this before moving the card to **done**.
